 `dots`, `busy`, `status`, `queued` > [!note] Why the two are computed differently
 `dots`, `busy`, `status`, `queued` > The egg's minutes are independent, so a window's summed z² is exactly chi-square: the original dot's math. GCP 2.0's minute values are a rolling statistic, not a chi-square, so they are ranked; control: the 1 h index alone gives 5.0 / 5.0 / 30.0 / 50.0 / 5.0 / 5.1 % per band. The egg's dot crosses band edges four to five times as often as GCP's smoothed one.
